  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday) \nIssued at 1229 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nThe latest RRFS suggests there is potential for some spotty\nafternoon showers and storms mainly across the south on Monday\nafternoon, again in the deep layer moist plume in the vicinity of\nwhat is left from the back door front. There is more uncertainty\nthough with upper heights expected to be rising by this time, but\nstill worth mentioning given outdoor plans folks may have on the \nholiday.\n\nUpper heights will continue to rise through the middle of the\nweek, with Tuesday and Wednesday expected to have headline-worthy\nhot and dry weather.\n\nA weak front is expected to drop down into Kansas on Wednesday,\nwith rain/storm chances returning to the forecast Wednesday night\ninto Thursday across NE OK and NW AR. The more optimistic GFS\nactually brings the likely outflow-reinforced boundary through the\nforecast area Thursday while the more pessimistic EC stalls the\nboundary near the KS/MO borders. The more aggressive solution\ncould also bring rain/storm chances and relatively cooler temps\ninto Friday as was reflected in the latest model blend (NBM) \nforecast.\n\nLooking even farther out, solutions vary quite a bit on timing but\na fall cold front is reflected at some point during the latter\nhalf of the month. We just have to get there.\n\nLacy",
